`defer` executes at function return, not block end. Your code queues all the `Close()` calls until the function exits, so every file stays open simultaneously. 

You run out of file descriptors because all open handles exist at once in memory. The loop doesn't free them as it iterates—it just stacks more defer statements.

Fix: call `Close()` explicitly in each iteration, or wrap the open/defer in an inner function so defer fires per iteration:

```go
for _, f := range files {
    func() {
        fh, _ := os.Open(f)
        defer fh.Close()
    }()
}
```
